      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 The Authors. Pain Practice © 2011 World Institute of Pain.",
        "AbstractText": "We report the successful use of low-dose ketamine infusion for treating a severe episode of painful myoclonus in the lower extremities, associated with opioid-induced hyperalgesia (OIH), in a patient who was receiving long-term, high dose intrathecal hydromorphone therapy. A low-dose ketamine infusion immediately relieved the painful myoclonus. It also enabled a reduction in the intrathecal opioid dosage leading to a resolution of the acute symptoms attributed to OIH."
      },
